userStories.description:
**Goal** — Introduce the read-only feature-state data model and aggregate spec, PRD, run and local branch state.

**Motivation** — Today a chat session has no tool or instruction that points it at `.nax/features/<name>/`, the PRD, the last run or the published PR, so it cannot answer "where does feature X stand" without the user walking it through the files.

**Approach** — New `src/chat/workflow/feature-state.ts` with the `FeatureStateOptions`, `FeatureState` and `WorkflowStateList` types, the two limits, `_featureStateDeps` (`git`, `isProcessAlive`), and `readFeatureState` filling `name`, `spec`, `prd`, `run`, `branch` and warnings 1-3 as described in Design. In this story `workflow` is always `null` and `lastRunLog` is always `null`; US-003 fills them. `status.json` is read through `readStatusFile`. Tests go in a new `test/unit/chat/workflow/feature-state.test.ts`, using a temp-dir fixture repo with real files and stubbed `git` and `isProcessAlive`.

Paths under `.nax/features` are built only with `featureDir` / `featuresDir`, because `check:feature-dir-ssot` bans open-coded `.nax/features` paths. `spec` is `relative(repoRoot, join(featureDir(repoRoot, name), "spec.md"))`. Resolve that spec first, then `.nax/specs/<name>.md`, else null. Read PRD with loadPRD and select branchName plus total/passed/failed/pending from countStories; missing PRD means prd and branch null. The shared status reader is imported via `../../execution/status-file-read`, never via `@/execution`. A missing, non-JSON or shape-rejected status file yields run null without warning; valid run fields come from run metadata, cost and progress, with alive from the injected process check.

Git probes, run in `repoRoot` through an injectable `_featureStateDeps.git` (default `gitWithTimeout`). A `branchName` that is empty or starts with `-` is never passed to git. Its branch fields take their negative values, because a leading `-` would be read as an option:
- `exists`: `rev-parse --verify --quiet refs/heads/<branch>` exits 0;
- `current`: `symbolic-ref --short HEAD` stdout trimmed equals the branch;
- `upstream`: `rev-parse --abbrev-ref <branch>@{upstream}` stdout trimmed when it exits 0, else null.
A git probe exiting non-zero, timing out or throwing makes only that field negative (exists false, current false, upstream null), with no warning. No git call is made without a PRD branch.

Warnings, in this order when several apply:
1. `prd.json unreadable: <message>` when `prd.json` exists but `loadPRD` throws;
2. `prd has <R> stories left but execution.maxIterations is <M>; pass -m <R> to nax run (nax#2706)` when `R = prd.pending` is greater than `maxIterations`. Only pending stories are eligible: `getNextStory` skips `passed`, `failed`, `regression-failed` and the other terminal states (`src/prd/index.ts:203-210`), and the run loop stops at `maxIterations` iterations (`unified-executor.ts:177`). Retries only add iterations, so `-m <R>` is a floor;
3. `run <id> is marked running but its process is gone` when `status.json` says `running` and the pid is not alive.

US-005 validates model-supplied names with validateFeatureName before any reads and translates validation/unknown-feature failures into ToolResult errors. This reader builds feature paths with featureDir; do not add a stricter validateFeatureName filter to the featureDir-based directory enumeration assigned to US-003, because the existing validators accept different name sets. Reuse existing path helpers rather than creating another feature-name grammar. Introduce the complete shared interfaces now; US-003 adds workflow/log aggregation and implements the list reader before US-005 consumes it.

**Scope** — In: shared types/limits, `_featureStateDeps.git` and `.isProcessAlive`, feature artifact reads, run projection, branch probes and warnings 1-3. Out: workflow verdicts, log discovery and list implementation (US-003), instructions (US-004), tool validation/error formatting and barrel exports (US-005), CLI composition (US-006). Feature-level boundaries: Fixing nax#2706 (silent stop at `maxIterations`); this feature only warns about it. Reading `naxCommit` from run logs, and spec layouts other than `.nax/features/<name>/spec.md` and `.nax/specs/<name>.md`.

**Interface** — verbatim data contract:
```typescript
export interface FeatureStateOptions {
  readonly repoRoot: string;
  /** `~/.nax/<projectKey>` (or the configured outputDir). */
  readonly outputDir: string;
  /** Resolved `config.execution.maxIterations`. */
  readonly maxIterations: number;
}

export interface FeatureState {
  readonly name: string;
  /** Repo-relative path of `.nax/features/<name>/spec.md` or `.nax/specs/<name>.md`; null when neither exists. */
  readonly spec: string | null;
  readonly prd: { readonly branchName: string; readonly total: number; readonly passed: number;
                  readonly failed: number; readonly pending: number } | null;
  /** From `.nax/features/<name>/status.json`. */
  readonly run: { readonly id: string; readonly status: string; readonly startedAt: string;
                  readonly alive: boolean; readonly spent: number;
                  readonly passed: number; readonly total: number } | null;
  /** From the newest readable `workflow/<runId>/result.json`. */
  readonly workflow: { readonly runId: string; readonly step: string; readonly outcome?: string;
                       readonly url?: string; readonly ci?: string;
                       readonly openItems: number; readonly firstOpenItems: readonly string[] } | null;
  /** Present only when `prd` is present (the branch name comes from it). */
  readonly branch: { readonly name: string; readonly exists: boolean; readonly current: boolean;
                     readonly upstream: string | null } | null;
  /** Newest `<outputDir>/features/<name>/runs/*.jsonl` file name without extension, excluding `latest.jsonl`. */
  readonly lastRunLog: string | null;
  readonly warnings: readonly string[];
}

export interface WorkflowStateList {
  readonly features: readonly FeatureState[];
  /** Feature directories beyond the list limit. */
  readonly omitted: number;
}

export const WORKFLOW_STATE_LIST_LIMIT = 10;
export const FIRST_OPEN_ITEMS_LIMIT = 5;

export function readFeatureState(name: string, options: FeatureStateOptions): Promise<FeatureState>;
export function readWorkflowStateList(options: FeatureStateOptions): Promise<WorkflowStateList>;
```
